{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent exact-SHA review: FAIL\n\nCandidate: 05ea2fe764dfb520ee594034270614aff5d8decb\nParent: c8af0eb82f2656b1102a137169bdb436cb2872bd\nImmutable audit base: d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84\nReviewer session: amebic-desecrated-joey (fa73-8df6-6322-45fd)\n\nBlocking semantic findings:\n\n1. `criterion_preview.py::D:module@1-34` and `criterion_preview.py::C:preview_criterion@107-109` (final `src/rebar/llm/workflow/criterion_preview.py:1-6` and `:74-75`) say synchronous previews are bounded and that `preview_criterion` keeps the editor responsive. The executable does not have that timing contract: `preview_criterion` uses `ThreadPoolExecutor` as a context manager, whose exit waits for the worker after `future.result(timeout=...)` raises. A focused reproduction with a 0.050s budget returned only after 0.360s. `preview_or_job` is the bounded endpoint path because it uses `thread.join(timeout)` and retains the live job. Correct the two condensed blocks to reserve the bounded/responsive claim for `preview_or_job`; do not describe direct `preview_criterion` as bounded unless executable behavior changes in a separately scoped ticket.\n\n2. `executor.py::D:resolve_value@284-289` (final `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py:234-237`) narrows the documented expression namespaces to step/input and environment expressions, omitting the supported `${{ secrets.<name> }}` namespace. `_resolve_one` resolves `_SECRET_RE`, and the focused consumer resolves `${{ secrets.S }}` successfully. Mention secret expressions alongside step/input/environment expressions so the condensed API contract remains complete.\n\n3. `gates/code-review.yaml::Y@2-15` (final `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml:2-6`) says verification, decision, and coaching remain deterministic. Only Pass 3 is a deterministic scripted decision. Pass 2 is an agent step configured with `temperature: 0`; Pass 4 coaching is also an agent step and has no temperature override, so it uses provider-default sampling. Restore the narrower claim that the decision stays deterministic and escalation cannot change the verdict; do not label coaching deterministic.\n\nAll structural evidence was otherwise green: exact HEAD/parent and 11-path scope, 99-block immutable prose/runtime/directive oracle, exact directive preservation, comment hygiene, diff integrity, commit-ticket/DCO/Change-Id checks, editor build with committed dist unchanged, and 191 focused tests. Per operator direction, no full `make verify` was run. Because at least one block fails semantic review, this review attaches exactly zero TSV PASS rows. Amend the prose only, then request a fresh independent review of the new exact SHA."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788987175830398001,"uuid":"ca7a9424-ced3-4947-86d6-b4a39b428b19"}